{"name":"Eat Your Peas","hex":"#80987a","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To ingest.","To consume a meal."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something to be eaten; a meal; a food item."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eat"},{"term":"your","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["Belonging to you; of you; related to you (singular; one owner).","Belonging to you; of you; related to you (plural; more owners)."]},{"part":"Contraction","definitions":["Misspelling of you're."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/your"},{"term":"peas","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of pea"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peas"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eat Your Peas","blocks":[{"text":"Eat Your Peas is the third and final album of material taken from the popular Australian radio show Martin/Molloy, by comedians Tony Martin and Mick Molloy. The album peaked at number 27 on the ARIA Charts and was certified platinum. At the ARIA Music Awards of 1999, the album won Best Comedy Release; their third time winning that category."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f1/Eat_Your_Peas_by_Martin_Molloy.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eat_Your_Peas","wikidata":"Q5331249"},{"title":"You","blocks":[{"text":"In Modern English, the word \"you\" is the second-person pronoun. It is grammatically plural, and was historically used only for the dative case, but in most modern dialects is used for all cases and numbers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/You","wikidata":"Q1165897"},{"title":"Pea","blocks":[{"text":"Pea is a pulse or fodder crop, but the word often refers to the seed or sometimes the pod of this flowering plant species. Peas are eaten as a vegetable. The pea is native to the Mediterranean region and southwest Asia, and cultivated nearly